{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And if you walk with Me בקרי.</b> This is the way of the Torah: when a person's affairs prosper and turn out well, he should reflect upon himself and take to heart that it is the lovingkindness of HaShem, may He be exalted — not on account of his merit and good deeds, as it is written (Deuteronomy 9:5): ״לא בצדקתך וביושר לבבך״. And when troubles and chance occurrences befall him, he should confess his transgression to HaShem, and consider that it is nothing but from the side of his sin, and not attribute them to chance; for if he attributes this to chance, the Holy One, blessed be He, will add to him more of that same chance. And this is what it says: ״ואם באלה לא תוסרו לי והלכתם עמי קרי והלכתי אף אני עמכם בקרי״, and likewise it says further: ״ואם בזאת לא תשמעו לי והלכתם עמי בקרי והלכתי עמכם בחמת קרי״ — that is to say, I will pour it out upon you in wrath."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:28:47.153437956Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}